\title{The exactness reviews and the choice of practical exactness}
\taxon{Session}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{machine}
\tag{reference-engine}
\meta{harness}{Claude Code}
\meta{model-id}{claude-fable-5-2}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The last phase of 2026-11-24 began when the machine was [taken back as the default engine](ses-CVTE). It asked one question from several sides: what would it take for the default configuration to give the official verdict on every input, and is that the right contract. Every review here judged against the official checker of Lean v4.36.0 run on the export, never against the reference engine.}

\ul{
\li{\strong{The wrong accepts and their fix.} Seven shapes, findings E1-F1 to E1-F7, with one root: the official kernel types a bound variable by its binder's declared type, and the machine typed it by the value in its slot, which can be a type that is only convertible. The fix gives bound variables their declared type (typed bindings), restricts the expected-type rule to one domain value, and added 78 hostile exports. It cost nothing measurable in warm wall clock. One shape is intrinsic to a machine on values and stays. See [inference shortcuts and typed bindings](design-inference-shortcuts), [the decision](dec-0DSI) and [the insight](ins-AAXM).}
\li{\strong{The shortcuts.} \src{docs/design/review/soundness-shortcuts.md}: the two proof-comparison options that [the profiles](ses-JRSD) priced are sound with respect to Lean's type theory as implemented. Every equation they assume is derivable, under the precondition that both sides are well typed, which the machine's inference establishes. Where they differ from the official verdict, the official checker accepts a proof of the same statement once the congruence step is written out as a term. See [the shortcuts](design-proof-comparison-shortcuts) and [the decision](dec-GL11).}
\li{\strong{The default set.} \src{docs/design/review/soundness-default-set.md}: the ten switches that had entered the default set without an adversarial review, attacked with 423 new exports, 200 of them random programs. No accept of an underivable statement. Six findings of accepts of derivable statements that the official checker rejects, one of them in the reference engine, with one root that no gate could see: the official \code{\verb~|is_def_eq~} is not a function of its two arguments, because one of its caches is read by cheap calls and written only by full ones. One switch, \code{k2}, gave a wrong accept with its default thresholds and [stays off](dec-MOCU). See [the review method](design-adversarial-review), [the insight](ins-PO1G) and the rule that followed, [no switch enters a default set without such a pass](dec-QN1O).}
\li{\strong{The reference engine.} \src{docs/design/review/reference-caches.md}: an audit of the oracle's own caches after one of those findings was an accept of the reference engine. The loader drops metadata nodes and a flag of let bindings that are part of the official term identity; the official verdict can depend on whether a subterm is one export record or two, through a pointer test, which no store that identifies equal terms can reproduce; and admission of inductive types keeps caches that the official kernel discards. All are accepts of derivable statements. See [the caches of the reference engine](design-reference-caches), [the example of the duplicated record](ex-7CCC) and [the open problem of the strict mode](prob-1YXM).}
}

\p{\strong{The decision.} With these findings the question was put to the maintainer as strict or practical exactness for the default, and the answer was practical: never an accept of an underivable statement, the official verdict on every real input, everything the official checker accepts is accepted, and an accept of a derivable statement that the official checker rejects only through its own incompleteness, non-transitivity, cache order or object identity is tolerated and written down. It is recorded in [standing policies](standing-policies); the classes that are tolerated are in [accepted risks](accepted-risks) and \src{docs/design/review/official-divergence.md}. In this journal: [the decision](dec-TQSI), [the exactness contract](design-exactness-contract), [the divergence classes](design-official-divergence), [metadata is declined only in the strict mode](dec-USLM), and the lesson for the gates, [a gate that compares with our own engine cannot see a divergence both engines share](ins-SJW4).}

\p{\strong{What followed the same evening.} One launcher option was wired to select the policy: practical is the default, and strict means the reference engine with its exactness-only behaviour, among it the decline of metadata in declarations and the official second pass where the verdict depends on object identity. The hostile suite of the machine got a kind per row: a row marked as tolerated demands the official verdict or an accept, every other row the official verdict. The gate for a default configuration runs a distribution exactly as a user does and judges it against official verdicts only. The second pass of the adversarial review attacked the candidate default, the default set with eager reduction and the two shortcuts, on 987 hostile exports with official verdicts, and found no accept of an underivable statement.}

\p{\strong{State at the end of the day.} The reference engine is the default engine. The launcher's policy option and its new defaults are published: \code{\verb~|-X policy=practical|strict~}, pipelined loading for parallel runs, two scanner threads for large inputs and an automatic worker count; see \src{rlvm-main/README.md}. The hostile suite of the machine holds the rows of every review, 1,189 in all, each with its official verdict and its kind. The review's condition for making the machine the default, no accept of an underivable statement in the candidate, is met. Still to come were the publication with the machine as default and its gate, the warm measurements that decide whether the shortcuts are on by default, the fix of the compiled code's decline of a valid unit (finding S3-F7), and a rule for the one known case in which transparent metadata makes RLVM reject what the official checker accepts, see [accepted risks](accepted-risks).}

